From: Kernel security backport review <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] iomap: release pages on atomic size rejection

Adapt to the older non-bounce iomap_dio_bio_iter. Release successfully
extracted pages before dropping the rejected atomic bio, preserving the
existing zero-tail and iterator re-expansion behavior.

CVE: CVE-2026-72370
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/681e452683b69a8e1a571cba0f238f8ceacf55d2]

diff --git a/fs/iomap/direct-io.c b/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
--- a/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
+++ b/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
@@ -470,6 +470,7 @@
 			 * bio_iov_iter_get_pages() returns an error, above.
 			 */
 			ret = -EINVAL;
+			bio_release_pages(bio, false);
 			bio_put(bio);
 			goto zero_tail;
 		}
